## P18-V01 Remoting GO_AWAY wrapper tryLock parity — 2026-10-24

- Code commit: `3b7cb5d2 fix(remoting): match GoAway wrapper trylock`.
- `ClientInner` now keeps weakly cached per-address wrapper locks. Current
  connection lookup reads under the wrapper lock; a GO_AWAY response tries a
  nonblocking write lock and, on contention, checks whether the generation
  changed. Contention with the same generation skips retirement/retry. A
  replacement or an already-retired generation remains eligible for the
  shared retry path. Socket-close cleanup with no current entry still retains
  the existing retry behavior.
- Added `go_away_try_lock_skips_current_channel_and_retries_replaced_channel`
  to cover same-generation lock contention and replacement routing.
- Focused Remoting gates passed: all-feature package tests (147 unit, 9 codec,
  1 fuzz-regression, 7 security, 109 transport, 20 doctests), strict
  all-target/all-feature Remoting Clippy, and the GO_AWAY transport subset
  (84 matching cases). A first full Remoting attempt exposed five regressions
  when no current map entry followed socket-close cleanup; that branch was
  corrected to preserve the pinned Java post-close retry and the rerun passed.

