## P18-V02 direct property decoder fuzz seeds — 2026-10-24

- Code commit: `67ee9ec4 test(remoting): fuzz encoded property strings`.
- The bounded deterministic smoke now collects unique encoded property
  strings from the invoked Java message fixture and mutates each 16 ways,
  including byte flips, truncation, U+0001/U+0002 separator edits, and
  control/invalid suffixes. The regression requires nonzero property seed and
  decoder counts; the example reports both counts.
- Focused fuzz regression and smoke passed: 163 frame seeds, 11 message seeds,
  11 property seeds, 2,960 total mutations, 564 frame decodes, 192 message
  decodes, and 176 property decodes. The full Remoting all-feature suite
  passed (147 unit, 9 codec, 1 fuzz-regression, 7 security, 109 transport,
  and 20 doctests). Strict all-target/all-feature Remoting Clippy, formatting,
  and diff checks passed.
- This closes the direct property-seed coverage gap in P18-V02 only. Broad
  P18-V01 reconciliation and native Windows/current remote Ubuntu evidence
  remain open; no push or remote CI ran, and the Phase 19-owned worktree paths
